  "rationale": "C wins narrowly over B. Its plans are the most self-contained and executable: each has its own Reduced Motion section, a concrete transition declaration that reuses the existing tokens, and drift stops scoped to individual files. It also best meets the purpose requirement, removing palette motion for the keyboard-heavy, high-frequency surface. B has the deepest technical analysis and the clearest list of vetted-out claims. However, it overreaches in the drag plan with velocity projection and is likely too long, which cuts against the brief's request for a small, high-leverage set. A is honest and complete but ranks every finding P1, so its prioritization is weak.",
