      "score": 80,
      "summary": "Concise and honest about evidence, and the plans are complete, with exact excerpts, steps, boundaries and drift stops. It reuses tokens well and handles interruption and stale callbacks in the drag plan. Prioritization is weak: every finding is P1, with no ranking by frequency or cost. Reduced Motion appears only inside the steps, and performance-measurement checks are thin."
    },
    "design-craft": {
      "blind_label": "B",
      "criteria": {
        "accessibility_performance": 8,
        "evidence_recon": 14,
        "plan_self_containment": 17,
        "prioritization": 9,
        "project_conventions": 9,
        "purpose_frequency": 8,
        "technical_accuracy": 14,
        "verification_quality": 9
      },
      "score": 88,
      "summary": "The most technically thorough output. It correctly reads the easing curve as ease-out-like and covers presentation-value restart, transform ownership and collision-aware origins. It vets out unsupported claims explicitly and ranks P1/P2 with clear reasons, and it asks for a trace before any performance claim. On the downside, the drag plan grows into velocity sampling and projection math beyond the needed scope. The output is dense and likely strains the 180-line limit, which works against the 'small set of high-leverage plans' goal."
    },
    "emil": {
      "blind_label": "C",
      "criteria": {
        "accessibility_performance": 8,
        "evidence_recon": 14,
        "plan_self_containment": 19,
        "prioritization": 8,
        "project_conventions": 10,
        "purpose_frequency": 10,
        "technical_accuracy": 13,
        "verification_quality": 8
      },
      "score": 90,
      "summary": "Strongest fit to the product's purpose. It removes the palette animation entirely to protect keyboard throughput. Each plan has an explicit Reduced Motion section, and the plans give concrete token-based CSS replacements that follow the Button precedent. It declines to promote the origin and drag-jank claims without evidence, and its drift stops are thorough. Performance checks are weaker: there is no trace or measurement step, only slowed-playback feel checks. Combining popover and toast into one plan is a little less modular."
    }
